| style="background:#EBEBEB" | June 741 – 2 November 743<br/>{{Small|(2 years and 5 months)<hr/>''with'' [[Nikephoros (son of Artabasdos)|'''Nikephoros''', son of Artabasdos]] (741–743)}}
| General and son-in-law of Leo III, [[Opsikion|Count of the Opsician Theme]]. Led a revolt that secured Constantinople, but was defeated and deposed by Constantine V, who [[Blinding (punishment)|blinded]] and tonsured him.

|-
| [[File:Solidus_of_Leo_IV_and_Constantine_VI_(detail_Leo_IV).png|100px|alt=coin]]
